#: includes/admin.php:646
msgid "Working on the site?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:647
msgid "Open everything for a set time instead of leaving a wide setting on. A session lifts the access level to published pages, makes synced patterns editable, allows dynamic data and brings theme building blocks, templates and navigation menus into scope. Other non-public post types, customer data above all, stay a tick somebody makes on purpose. It is also the only time the agent may publish and upload images: opening a session is deciding that what gets built in it may go live. It closes itself when the time is up; the settings below are what the site falls back to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:652
msgid "A session widens what the agent may do with the tools it already has. It does not add tools: the tool list follows the level below, because MCP clients read it once when they connect and never ask again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:659
msgid "Close now"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: name of the drafts level, 2: name of the widest level
#: includes/admin.php:671
#, php-format
msgid "The level is \"Read only\", so the agent has no write tools and a session cannot give it any. Set the level to \"%1$s\" or \"%2$s\" to let the agent write during a session."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:681
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:686
msgid "What the agent may do"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:702
msgid "No level lets the agent publish or upload images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:703
msgid "Both are possible only during a work session you open (see above). Deleting and changing settings are never possible. Tools the level does not allow are not registered at all, so the agent never sees them, and a work session does not add any. Every write creates a revision."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:705
