#: includes/admin.php:740
msgid "This post type usually holds other people's data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:741
msgid "personal data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:750
msgid "Public post types and pages are already in scope. Everything else is listed here — a theme's headers, footers, hooks and content templates among them. Adding one is a real decision: those apply to every page at once, the way a synced pattern does, so a change there is not confined to the page being edited. In code, the wpmcp_allowed_post_types filter does the same thing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:752
msgid "The ones marked \"personal data\" are a different question."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:753
msgid "Orders, subscriptions and form entries hold your customers' names and addresses. Ticking one lets the agent read them. That is rarely what you want from a tool for editing pages, and on a shop it is a decision your privacy policy has to cover."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:758
msgid "Dynamic data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:763
msgid "Blocked — pages containing dynamic data stay read-only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:764
msgid "Allowed — the agent may save them too"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:781
msgid "This setting cannot take effect on this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:786
msgid "Some block libraries refuse to save a page holding dynamic data unless the account has unfiltered_html — the capability that permits storing arbitrary HTML and JavaScript. That would be the widest permission in a role that deliberately cannot publish, delete, upload or change settings, so it is never given to the role. When this is allowed, it is granted for the length of one save and taken away again, and a write that newly introduces a script tag, an inline event handler or a javascript: URL is still refused. Every such save is marked in the activity log."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:791
msgid "Synced patterns"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:796
msgid "Hidden — the agent cannot see what is inside them"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:797
msgid "Readable — the agent can look inside but not change them"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:798
msgid "Editable — the agent may change them"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:813
msgid "A synced pattern appears on every page that embeds it, so changing one changes all of them at once — and a pattern has no draft state. The dry run says how many pieces of content are affected before anything is saved."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:818
msgid "Keep the activity log"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:823
msgid "days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:825
msgid "Older entries are deleted once a day. 0 keeps them forever. Every read, dry run and refusal is an entry, so on a site the agent works on daily the log grows by thousands of rows a month."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:856
msgid "Activity log"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:858
msgid "Every call the agent made, newest first: what it read, what it tried, what it saved and what was refused. Saves link to the revision they left, so the change can be compared and undone in the editor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:862
msgid "Entries are kept forever."
msgstr ""

